# OnTrak first-boot settings.
#
# The installer ISO drops this file at first boot (see infra/installer/README.md).
# It is optional: with no file, the defaults below are used.
#
# Every setting here can also be passed as an environment variable to
#   sudo /usr/local/sbin/ontrak-firstboot.sh --force
#
# Copy to /etc/ontrak/firstboot.env, edit, then re-run the script (or reboot).

# --------------------------------------------------------------- checkout ----
# The repository to install. A private remote needs ONTRAK_GIT_TOKEN: the script
# tries the anonymous clone first and only then the token.
ONTRAK_REPO_URL=https://github.com/innotelinc/OnTrak.git
ONTRAK_BRANCH=main
ONTRAK_REPO_DIR=/opt/ontrak

# A GitHub token with read access to the repository, used only if the anonymous
# clone fails. Leave unset for a public remote. Never commit a real value.
#ONTRAK_GIT_TOKEN=github_pat_…

# The admin login the interactive installer created, if it is not the first
# non-system account. It is added to the incus and docker groups.
#ONTRAK_INSTALL_LOGIN=ontrak

# ------------------------------------------------------------- hypervisor ----
# Passed straight to infra/bootstrap-host.sh. The default (dir) is correct but
# slow for a real class: clones are full copies. On a machine with a spare
# device, zfs or btrfs with snapshots is what makes provisioning quick.
#ONTRAK_STORAGE_DRIVER=zfs
#ONTRAK_STORAGE_SOURCE=/dev/nvme1n1
#ONTRAK_STORAGE_POOL=default
#ONTRAK_NETWORK=ontrak0
#ONTRAK_NET_CIDR=10.20.0.1/24
#ONTRAK_DOMAIN=ontrak.lab

# ------------------------------------------------------------ range content --
# 1 to also build the golden Windows image and every scenario template as part of
# the first boot. Hours of work, and the Windows media is not redistributable, so
# it is off by default — run `make golden && make templates` when you want it.
ONTRAK_BUILD_TEMPLATES=0

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Secrets the stack reads from .env are *not* set here. Generated local values
# are created by `make secrets` during the first boot; production values come
# from Cerulean Vault by reference (see .env.example). To put OnTrak's names on
# the estate afterwards: cd /opt/ontrak && make provision
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
